<title>FRANCE: French Aug M3 money supply grew 0.6 percent.</title>
<headline>French Aug M3 money supply grew 0.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France gave the following money supply figures (the year-on-year change is expressed as an average centred on the previous month)</p>
<p> Money measure  Billions   Monthly change    12-month change</p>
<p>(end-Aug)	(unadj)	(adjusted)	   Jul	 Jun</p>
<p>    M1	    1,643.8	  1.6		 6.1	 6.1</p>
<p>    M2	    3,123.6	  1.0		 7.8	 7.7</p>
<p>    M3	    5,306.4	  0.6		 0.3	 1.0</p>
<p>    M4	    5,410.2	  0.5		 0.8	 1.5</p>
<p>Investment</p>
<p>    P1	    1,818.5	  1.3		18.4	18.0</p>
<p> Credit measure		billions	   Year-on-Year change</p>
<p>  (end-Jul)		    (unadj)	   Jul     Jun	May</p>
<p> Total domestic debt	10,824.8	   3.3     3.7	4.8</p>
<p> Total credits to economy  6,348.0	  -0.6     0.0	2.0</p>
<p> Bank credits to economy   3,559.0	  -0.7     0.3     -0.2</p>
<p>The Bank originally said M3 fell 0.2 percent in July from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>The central bank is targeting M3 growth of roughly five percent a year on average over the next few years.</p>
<p>It is using total domestic debt as a secondary monitoring tool.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
